\title{Stock}
\date{2026-06-12T21:29:43Z}
\import{swarm-macros}

\p{Similarly, there is a special \sf{stock} directive which requires a certain number of a specific entity to be in the inventory, with a similarly straightforward typing rule:

\rules{
    \swty{\Gamma}{\stock{n}{e}}{\Cmd{(\varnothing,\varnothing,#{\lbag e \mapsto n \rbag})}{\Unit}}{\varnothing}
}

Similar to \sf{require}, #{n} and #{e} must be a natural number literal and an entity name literal, respectively.
}
